{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791581129,"nonce":"QRDc9ZRRwUb5lmfhPHIAYAeXUhA=","message":"Direction update (user, 2026-10-09): needed as the way to stop using Stateful for changing children, and For has to take iterators.\n\nDone so far: signal-bound when() (696122f2c37171297755be98b82ce84ad6b91bee). It builds the children its closure adds either way and shows them while the condition holds (display none and back, no wrapper, no rebuild). It is the cheap form of Show; lazy branches and lists still need the machinery below.\n\nRead from ashui (ashui/haxe/ashui/ui/For.hx and Show.hx, 85 lines together):\n- each() is tracked like a computed and returns the list; item(value) builds a row; reconciled at the next flush.\n- They are fragments with no box of their own: rows are laid out as the placing element's own children, so its direction, gap and alignment apply to them.\n- Each row is built under its own Owner; a surviving row keeps its element, a removed one is disposed with everything it created.\n- Matching is by == with a linear scan (quadratic).\n\nGaps found in Blinc:\n1. No fragment. taffy 0.14 has no display: contents (Display is Block, FlowRoot, Flex, Grid, None). Either a host form (the container Div owns the region from an index on) or a fragment kind in LayoutTree flattened into the nearest real parent's taffy children, with paint, hit test and events seeing the flattened list.\n2. No owner. Building a row creates signals, computeds, bindings and keyed state with nothing to dispose them together (compare 483c864).\n3. Row identity. StableNodeId comes from parent id plus sibling index, so a middle insert or remove moves every later row. Rows need an explicit key.\n4. No in-place splice of one subtree at an index; process_pending_subtree_rebuilds rebuilds a parent's children.\n\nIterator form: each: Fn() -\u003e impl IntoIterator\u003cItem = T\u003e, tracked like a computed; key: Fn(\u0026T) -\u003e K with K: Hash + Eq (a map, not a scan); item: Fn(T) -\u003e impl ElementBuilder built under a row scope. A row whose key survives keeps its node and scope; order is reconciled.","files":null}]}